lay_name": "Zen Stargazer", "keywords": ["astronomy", "stargazing", "stars", "planets", "constellations"], "long_description": "Zen Stargazer is a mixed-reality stargazing experience for Meta Quest. Your room stays real; the sky above follows your chosen time and location.\n\nPOINT TO LEARN\nAim the right controller at the sky to identify stars, planets, nebulae, and galaxies\u2014with short educational notes for bright landmarks.\n\nTIME & PLACE\nFollow live \u201cnow,\u201d or lock a custom observing time. Pick a city on the world map and the sky updates instantly\u2014great for rehearsing a meteor peak or revisiting an eclipse night.\n\nCONSTELLATIONS & DEEP SKY\nToggle constellation lines, the ecliptic, and selected deep-sky objects. Some targets include public-domain astronomy imagery for context.\n\nPLANETS & MOON\nExplore planet phases and moon illumination with a telescope-style view. Jump chips help you hop to previous or next related sky events.\n\nMETEOR SHOWERS & EVENT BOOK\nBrowse classic showers and key sky events. Shower notes explain what you\u2019ll see\u2014and that most showers are dust from a parent body (often a comet) entering Earth\u2019s atmosphere.\n\nPASSTHROUGH & FULL SKY\nUse the left stick to adjust how much real-world passthrough is revealed under the virtual sky; push further for a full-sphere / space view. Export a 360\u00b0 sky still to share.\n\nLANGUAGES\nUI and core content support Traditional Chinese, English, and Japanese\u2014switch anytime from the info pad.\n\nUse in a clear guardian boundary. Zen Stargazer is for learning and wonder; ephemerides are educational approximations\u2014not a substitute for professional almanacs.", "short_description": "Look up in mixed reality on Meta Quest. Point to learn stars, planets, and deep-sky objects. Scrub time, choose your observing site, follow meteor showers and eclipses. A left-hand info pad keeps the sky in reach\u2014\u7e41\u4e2d / English / \u65e5\u672c\u8a9e."}]}, "developer_nam